<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Baza</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Baza is a town in the province of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/granada">Granada</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/andalusia">Andalusia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>, on a high plateau in the north-east of the province, near the site of the Iberian town of Basti. Under Muslim rule it was an important town of the Nasrid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">Emirate</a> of Granada until the Catholic Monarchs took it after a long siege in 1489.</p></div>
